{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgWBZMEBZQ8VjoL47puvN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I haven't edited the spec yet. A person needs to decide this first.\n\n**Reasons:**\n\n1. **The spec is already `Status: accepted`** (`spec/2026-10-19-khach-khong-mat-viec.md:3`). Under the repo's rules I only write drafts. Changing the content of an accepted spec means changing a document a person has already approved, so a person has to decide it and commit it. That's how commit `65fae52` was done.\n2. **\"Dữ liệu trang web\" was chosen on purpose.** The change log at line 256 says: *\"2026-10-27 · F4 bước 1, tiêu chí 23: 'dữ liệu trình duyệt' → 'dữ liệu trang web', theo câu trên app (Linh chốt, Mai xác nhận đạt P4)\"*. Changing it would reverse a choice Linh and Mai made.\n3. **The spec would no longer match the app.** The app text at `app/index.html:32` says \"xoá dữ liệu trang web\", and `tests/static.test.js:25` pins that sentence. If only the spec changes, tiêu chí 23 no longer matches the app. Keeping them in line would mean changing `app/index.html` and that test too.\n\n**If you still want to change it**, here are the steps:\n- Get agreement from Linh, and from Mai for the P4 part.\n- Edit line 244 (tiêu chí 23) and line 74 (F4 bước 1, which uses the same wording) to say \"dữ liệu duyệt web\".\n- Add a line to the change log.\n- Change the app text and update `tests/static.test.js:25` in the same change, then run `bash scripts/check.sh`.\n- A person commits it.\n\nOnce Linh and Mai have agreed, tell me and I'll make the edits to the spec, app and test and run the check. I won't commit."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":591,"cache_read_input_tokens":37071,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":591},"output_tokens":603,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"